1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,448
My new mirror refuses to show my face. Instead, it displays every bad decision I am about to make today.

2
00:00:08,748 --> 00:00:17,148
At noon, the glass clouds over. It shows me dropping my coffee on a stranger's pristine white designer shoes.

3
00:00:17,448 --> 00:00:24,144
I hold my breath and refuse to move. I don't drop the cup. I actually beat the mirror's prediction.

4
00:00:24,444 --> 00:00:33,036
Proud of myself, I rush back home and stand before the glass again. I expect praise, but the mirror darkens.

5
00:00:33,336 --> 00:00:41,400
The surface ripples like water. A hand presses outward from the glass, leaving a cold fingerprint on the surface.

6
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:51,708
My reflection stops copying my movements entirely. It smiles a sad, knowing smile and taps frantically on the glass.

7
00:00:52,008 --> 00:00:59,064
Words scratch onto the lower corner from the inside. Letters of dust spelling out a warning I never wanted.

8
00:00:59,364 --> 00:01:05,868
It wasn't showing my future at all. It was showing the exact moment I stopped paying attention yesterday.

9
00:01:06,168 --> 00:01:12,936
I realize the truth too late. The mirror wasn't broken. It was holding a prisoner who tried to warn me.

10
00:01:13,236 --> 00:01:21,036
Now the glass is entirely empty. If the reflection escaped into my room, who is standing right behind me?
